            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0227" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1981-88v41/pg181"/>

                <head>58. Papers Prepared in the Department of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d58-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1982-06-25">June 25, 1982</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#section-heading #italic">PAPERS FOR SHULTZ BRIEFING BOOK</p>
                <p>1. Human Rights in the Administration’s Foreign Policy.</p>
                <p>2. Human Rights and the Communist Countries.</p>
                <p>3. Human Rights and Latin America.</p>
                <p>4. Human Rights and the Congress.</p>
                <p>5. State Department Role in Granting Political Asylum.</p>




                <xi:include href="d58-a1.xml" xpointer="d58-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d58-a2.xml" xpointer="d58-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d58-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d58-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Subject Files, Human Rights Files, 1979–1981, Lot
                    92D165, Briefing Papers for Sec-designate Shultz June 82. No classification marking. Drafted by Levitsky and cleared by Abrams. Papers 1 and 2 are printed as
                    attachments; 3, 4, and 5 are attached but not printed. All are undated.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
